## When to invoke

- Any change touching authentication, authorization, sessions, or token handling.
- Code that handles, parses, or stores user-supplied input — request bodies, query params, file uploads, webhook payloads.
- New external integrations, API consumers, or webhook receivers.
- Crypto, secrets, signing, or sensitive data flows — new or modified.
- Dependency additions or major version bumps on security-sensitive packages.
- Pre-release security pass on a feature before merge.

